                  "ref": "~sircmpwn/scdoc#28",
                  "subject": "[PATCH scdoc] Fix typo in scdoc.1.scd: 'This variables specifies' -> 'This variable specifies'",
                  "body": "Fix a grammar error in the SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH documentation: \r\n'This variables specifies' -> 'This variable specifies'\r\n\r\nThe rendered man page currently shows:\r\n\"This variables specifies the date\"\r\n\r\nThis is incorrect - \"variables\" should be the singular \"variable\".\r\n\r\nPatch follows:\r\n\r\n--- a/scdoc.1.scd\r\n+++ b/scdoc.1.scd\r\n@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@ _man_(7) style roff to the standard output.\r\n # ENVIRONMENT\r\n \r\n The scdoc utility supports the standard _SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH_ environment\r\n-variable for reproducible builds. This variables specifies the date in number\r\n+variable for reproducible builds. This variable specifies the date in number\r\n of seconds since the Unix epoch, see:\r\n https://reproducible-builds.org/specs/source-date-epoch/\r\n",
                  "status": "RESOLVED",
                  "resolution": "INVALID",
                  "submitter": {
                    "canonicalName": "~lechynte",
                    "id": 82960,
                    "updated": "2026-07-19T10:49:42.717328Z",
                    "username": "lechynte",
                    "email": "redacted@example.invalid",
                    "url": "https://sr.ht/~lechynte/",
                    "location": "Earth",
                    "bio": "Developer creating useful utilities and tools. Building entutils — a collection of everyday CLI tools. Interested in system programming, open source, and practical software."
                  },
